{
  "id": "GtaWantedLevelC02",
  "slug": "gta-wanted-level/c02",
  "chapter": "The rules",
  "topic": "What if you got a five-star wanted level in real life?",
  "script": [
    {
      "beat": "wake",
      "text": "It starts on a Tuesday. You wake up, and something is floating above your head. Five empty stars, in a little row, like a crown."
    },
    {
      "beat": "nobody sees",
      "text": "Mum doesn't see them. Your little sister Ellie doesn't see them. At school, your best friend Mo walks straight past them."
    },
    {
      "beat": "mirror",
      "text": "At breakfast, you wave your hand through them. Nothing. You check the bathroom mirror. Still there, very faint, like stickers on the glass."
    },
    {
      "beat": "rule one",
      "text": "By lunch, you've worked out the rules. Break any rule, even a tiny one, and a star fills in."
    },
    {
      "beat": "crack",
      "text": "You test it on the way home. You step on a crack in the sidewalk. Nothing. That's not a rule. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "beat": "rule two",
      "text": "If a police officer sees you while you have a star, they come for you, exactly like in a game. And if you run, you get another star."
    },
    {
      "beat": "rule three",
      "text": "One more thing. If you stay out of sight long enough, the stars flash, and fade away. At least, that's how it works at the start."
    }
  ],
